From 565cc1378b492a7423fc53141d62a5099b59cc53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael C. Ferguson" <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:19:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] usb: dwc2: host: do not mask XferCompl after a descriptor
 DMA completion

In descriptor DMA mode dwc2_hc_xfercomp_intr() hands a non-isochronous
completion to dwc2_hcd_complete_xfer_ddma() and then masks XferCompl
on the channel. By then the channel has been released, which already
cleared HCINTMSK, and the transaction queueing at the end of
dwc2_hcd_complete_xfer_ddma() may have assigned the same channel to
another QH and set its interrupt mask. If that QH is isochronous, its
XferCompl is masked, and a descriptor DMA isochronous channel is only
serviced on XferCompl until its session ends, so the stream stalls.

XferCompl is only unmasked for isochronous channels in this mode, and
isochronous completions already return without touching the mask.
Return for every descriptor DMA completion.

Fixes: dc4c76e7b22c ("staging: HCD descriptor DMA support for the DWC2 driver")
Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c
index a1a5988..ae2829e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_intr.c
@@ -977,11 +977,9 @@ static void dwc2_hc_xfercomp_intr(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg,
 	pipe_type = dwc2_hcd_get_pipe_type(&urb->pipe_info);
 
 	if (hsotg->params.dma_desc_enable) {
+		/* The channel may already serve another QH: leave its mask */
 		dwc2_hcd_complete_xfer_ddma(hsotg, chan, chnum, halt_status);
-		if (pipe_type == USB_ENDPOINT_XFER_ISOC)
-			/* Do not disable the interrupt, just clear it */
-			return;
-		goto handle_xfercomp_done;
+		return;
 	}
 
 	/* Handle xfer complete on CSPLIT */
-- 
